      "summary": "Tallinn: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 5",
      "content": "### Chapter 1: Tallinn: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Tallinn - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/tallinn-character.jpg)\n\nTallinn is one of Europe's best-preserved medieval trading cities, flourishing as a proud Hanseatic League port on the Gulf of Finland. The historic walled citadel of Vanalinn is divided between the limestone crest of Toompea Hill—seat of ancient Danish lords and bishops—and the Lower Town, where wealthy German guild merchants constructed magnificent gabled merchant houses, Gothic churches, and paved market squares.\n\n![Geographic location of Tallinn in Estonia](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/tallinn-map.png)\n\nA continuous two-kilometer circuit of stone walls punctuated by twenty-six conical red-roofed defensive towers—including Kiek in de Kök and Fat Margaret—surrounds the old city. In the Raekoja plats (Town Hall Square), the late-Gothic town hall with its historic Old Thomas weathervane presides over outdoor terraces and winter markets. The soaring spire of Saint Olaf's Church, once the tallest structure in the world, offers panoramic views across cobblestone alleys to the bustling Baltic harbor."
