      "summary": "Vilnius: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 5",
      "content": "### Chapter 3: Vilnius: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Vilnius - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/vilnius-character.jpg)\n\nNestled in a picturesque wooded river basin at the confluence of the Neris and Vilnia rivers, Vilnius is the historic capital of the Grand Duchy of Lithuania. Crowned atop a forested bluff is the red-brick Gediminas' Tower, the iconic surviving keep of the Upper Castle, from which sweeping panoramas open across one of Europe's largest preserved Old Towns, characterized by an astonishing profusion of baroque and neoclassical church spires.\n\n![Geographic location of Vilnius in Lithuania](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/vilnius-map.png)\n\nAmong the city's architectural masterpieces is the Church of Saint Anne, a flamboyant late-Gothic marvel of thirty-three varieties of red clay brick so delicate that Napoleon reportedly wished to carry it home to Paris in the palm of his hand. Across the river lies the quirky, self-declared bohemian Republic of Užupis, where artists, sculptors, and poets gather in riverside courtyards beneath playful bronze angels."
