      "summary": "Gdańsk: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 5",
      "content": "### Chapter 4: Gdańsk: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Gdańsk - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/gdansk-character.jpg)\n\nResting along the Motława River near the Baltic coast, Gdańsk was the maritime powerhouse and crown jewel of the Hanseatic League, controlling the export of Polish grain and Baltic amber to Western Europe. The Royal Way—stretching from the Golden Gate along Długa Street to the Long Market—is flanked by tall, slender burgher houses with ornate Mannerist and Renaissance gables, decorated with gilding, frescos, and heraldic crests.\n\n![Geographic location of Gdańsk in Poland](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/gdansk-map.png)\n\nDominating the historic riverside quays is the colossal Żuraw, a fifteenth-century wooden treadmill port crane used to load merchant ships and step masts. The cobblestone lane of Mariacka Street features elevated carved stone terraces (przedproża) with wrought-iron railings and gargoyle water spouts, where artisan workshops display exquisite Baltic amber jewelry beneath the massive brick buttresses of Saint Mary's Basilica."
