      "title": "Visby: The Desert Sanctuary",
      "summary": "Visby: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 5",
      "content": "### Chapter 6: Visby: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Visby - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/visby-character.jpg)\n\nPerched upon a limestone cliff overlooking the Baltic Sea on the island of Gotland, Visby was the supreme Baltic crossroads of the Hanseatic League during the twelfth to fourteenth centuries. The entire medieval city is enclosed within the Ringmuren, an intact three-and-a-half-kilometer limestone wall dating from 1288, punctuated by thirty-six defensive towers and monumental arched gates.\n\n![Geographic location of Visby in Sweden](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/visby-map.png)\n\nWithin the walls, winding cobblestone alleys lined with colorful low wooden cottages are famous for hundreds of climbing roses that bloom in summer, earning Visby the title 'City of Roses'. The skyline is uniquely punctuated by the romantic stone ruins of a dozen medieval Gothic churches—such as Saint Nicholas and Saint Karin—their roofless arches and tracery windows framing the northern sea sky beside the preserved twin towers of Saint Mary's Cathedral."
