      "title": "Uppsala: The Desert Sanctuary",
      "summary": "Uppsala: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 5",
      "content": "### Chapter 7: Uppsala: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Uppsala - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/uppsala-character.jpg)\n\nSituated along the gentle waters of the Fyris River, Uppsala is the historic ecclesiastical and intellectual capital of Sweden. Rising dramatically above the city is Uppsala Cathedral, Scandinavia's largest Gothic cathedral, whose twin red-brick spires soar one hundred and eighteen meters into the sky, housing the tombs of medieval Swedish kings and the botanical pioneer Carl Linnaeus.\n\n![Geographic location of Uppsala in Sweden](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/uppsala-map.png)\n\nAcross the university park stands the Gustavianum, the university's oldest surviving building, crowned by its unique seventeenth-century anatomical theatre with a wooden cupola. On the southern ridge, the imposing pink-and-terracotta Uppsala Castle overlooks lush botanical gardens, while students and scholars cycle along tree-lined riverside promenades and historic stone bridges crossing the Fyris."
