      "title": "Lund: The Desert Sanctuary",
      "summary": "Lund: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 5",
      "content": "### Chapter 9: Lund: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Lund - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/lund-character.jpg)\n\nFounded around 990 when the province of Scania was part of the Kingdom of Denmark, Lund is one of Scandinavia's oldest and most prestigious cultural cities. At its center stands Lund Cathedral, celebrated as the finest Romanesque building in the Nordic countries, constructed of dark gray sandstone with twin forty-five-meter towers called 'the boys of Lund'.\n\n![Geographic location of Lund in Sweden](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/lund-map.png)\n\nInside the cathedral, a remarkable fifteenth-century astronomical clock (Horologium Mirabile Lundense) chimes twice daily, prompting mechanical wooden figures of the Three Wise Men to parade past Mary and baby Jesus. Surrounding the cathedral, the cobblestone alleys of the historic Kulturen open-air museum and Lund University's ivy-covered library exude a timeless collegiate tranquility shaded by ancient beech trees."
