      "title": "Copenhagen: The Desert Sanctuary",
      "summary": "Copenhagen: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 5",
      "content": "### Chapter 10: Copenhagen: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Copenhagen - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/copenhagen-character.jpg)\n\nGracefully straddling the islands of Zealand and Amager on the Øresund strait, Copenhagen is the vibrant maritime capital of Denmark. Its most iconic postcard view is Nyhavn (New Harbor), a seventeenth-century canal lined on both sides by brightly painted gabled townhouses in sunny yellow, crimson, and royal blue, where historic wooden sailing ships moor outside lively quayside cafes.\n\n![Geographic location of Copenhagen in Denmark](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/copenhagen-map.png)\n\nThe city harmoniously blends royal baroque palaces like Amalienborg and Christiansborg with cutting-edge Nordic sustainable design and harbor baths where residents swim in crystal-clear sea water. Bicycles glide effortlessly across world-class bike bridges like the Circle Bridge, while the romantic gardens and historic wooden roller coaster of Tivoli Gardens glow under thousands of fairy lights in the heart of the city."
