      "summary": "Helsinki: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 5",
      "content": "### Chapter 11: Helsinki: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Helsinki - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/helsinki-character.jpg)\n\nSurrounded by the sparkling waters of the Gulf of Finland and an archipelago of over three hundred granite islands, Helsinki is famous as the White City of the North. At its neoclassical heart lies Senate Square, designed by Carl Ludvig Engel, crowned by the radiant Helsinki Cathedral whose stark white columns and emerald-green zinc domes gleam above monumental granite steps.\n\n![Geographic location of Helsinki in Finland](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/helsinki-map.png)\n\nIn the bustling Market Square (Kauppatori), orange tents sell fresh Baltic herring and forest berries while harbor ferries depart for Suomenlinna, the colossal eighteenth-century sea fortress spread across six interconnected islands. Helsinki's world-renowned design district showcases functionalist masterpieces by Alvar Aalto, alongside wood-fired public saunas where bathers plunge directly into the icy sea."
