      "summary": "Porvoo: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 5",
      "content": "### Chapter 12: Porvoo: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Porvoo - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/porvoo-character.jpg)\n\nSituated fifty kilometers east of Helsinki, Porvoo is Finland's second-oldest town, chartered in 1346. Its most iconic view is the picturesque row of red-ochre painted timber shore warehouses lining the tranquil Porvoonjoki river, originally painted red in the late eighteenth century in honor of the arrival of King Gustav III of Sweden.\n\n![Geographic location of Porvoo in Finland](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/porvoo-map.png)\n\nCobblestone streets wind gently up the hillside through Old Porvoo, past pastel wooden burgher houses with louvered shutters and courtyard gardens. At the crest of the hill stands the fourteenth-century Porvoo Cathedral with its distinctive steep red-and-white gabled facade, site of the 1809 Diet of Porvoo where Tsar Alexander I established Finland as an autonomous Grand Duchy."
