      "summary": "Turku: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 5",
      "content": "### Chapter 13: Turku: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Turku - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/turku-character.jpg)\n\nFounded in the late thirteenth century, Turku was the historic capital and intellectual cradle of Finland for over five hundred years under Swedish rule. Life in Turku revolves around the scenic Aura River, where pedestrian boulevards are lined with historic restaurant riverboats, leafy linden trees, and open-air cafes.\n\n![Geographic location of Turku in Finland](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/turku-map.png)\n\nNear the river mouth stands Turku Castle, a formidable gray granite fortress founded in 1280 that has witnessed centuries of Scandinavian royal rivalries and sieges. Upriver, the red-brick Turku Cathedral, considered the mother church of Finland, soars above the university park. Wooden sailing vessels cruise from Turku into the Archipelago Sea, the world's largest island maze with over twenty thousand granite skerries."
