      "title": "Rovaniemi: The Desert Sanctuary",
      "summary": "Rovaniemi: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 5",
      "content": "### Chapter 14: Rovaniemi: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Rovaniemi - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/rovaniemi-character.jpg)\n\nStraddling the Arctic Circle at the confluence of the Kemijoki and Ounasjoki rivers, Rovaniemi is the official hometown of Santa Claus and the urban gateway to Finnish Lapland. Rebuilt after World War II according to a master plan by architect Alvar Aalto shaped like reindeer antlers, the city features public buildings inspired by the harsh northern elements.\n\n![Geographic location of Rovaniemi in Finland](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/rovaniemi-map.png)\n\nSpanning the river is the Jätkänkynttilä (Lumberjack's Candle) Bridge, whose golden pylon flame glows against polar twilight. At the subterranean Arktikum science center, a glass tunnel extends toward the frozen river, offering front-row views of emerald and violet ribbons of Aurora Borealis dancing across the subarctic sky, while snow-laden taiga pine forests stretch infinitely into the polar wilderness."
