      "title": "Trondheim: The Desert Sanctuary",
      "summary": "Trondheim: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 5",
      "content": "### Chapter 15: Trondheim: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Trondheim - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/trondheim-character.jpg)\n\nFounded by Viking King Olav Tryggvason in 997 on the sheltered Trondheim Fjord, Trondheim (ancient Nidaros) was Norway's first medieval capital. Anchoring the city is Nidaros Cathedral, the northernmost medieval Gothic cathedral in the world, constructed of soapstone with an astonishing west facade filled with dozens of sculpted kings, saints, and gargoyles.\n\n![Geographic location of Trondheim in Norway](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/trondheim-map.png)\n\nCrossing the wooden Old Town Bridge (Gamle Bybro) leads into Bakklandet, a fairytale neighborhood of cobbled lanes lined with colorful seventeenth-century wooden houses. Overhanging the calm waters of the Nidelva River are rows of timber merchant warehouses (bryggene) painted in deep rust red, mustard yellow, and forest green, their foundations resting on stilts reflected in the fjord tide."
