      "prefix": "Chapter 16",
      "title": "Stavanger: The Desert Sanctuary",
      "summary": "Stavanger: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 5",
      "content": "### Chapter 16: Stavanger: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Stavanger - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/stavanger-character.jpg)\n\nNestled along the jagged coast of southwestern Norway, Stavanger is a vibrant maritime city framed by the dramatic waters of the Boknafjord and Lysefjord. In Gamle Stavanger (Old Stavanger), over one hundred and seventy immaculate eighteenth-century wooden cottages painted in brilliant white line narrow stone-paved alleys adorned with blooming flower boxes and antique street lamps.\n\n![Geographic location of Stavanger in Norway](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/stavanger-map.png)\n\nAt the city center stands the twelfth-century Stavanger Cathedral, Norway's oldest surviving cathedral, built of gray granite in the Anglo-Norman Romanesque style. Colorful modern street art covers the walls of the lively Øvre Holmegate district, nicknamed 'Fargegaten' (The Street of Colors), while catamarans depart from the harbor into the Lysefjord toward the dizzying six-hundred-meter vertical drop of Preikestolen (Pulpit Rock)."
