      "title": "Kilkenny: The Desert Sanctuary",
      "summary": "Kilkenny: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 5",
      "content": "### Chapter 18: Kilkenny: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Kilkenny - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/kilkenny-character.jpg)\n\nSituated on the banks of the River Nore in southeast Ireland, Kilkenny is known as the Marble City for its distinctive polished black limestone flagstones that glisten like marble in the rain. Dominating the river bend is the colossal twelfth-century Kilkenny Castle, a formidable Anglo-Norman stone fortress with three round drum towers set within fifty acres of rolling parkland.\n\n![Geographic location of Kilkenny in Ireland](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/kilkenny-map.png)\n\nThe Medieval Mile connects the castle to the thirteenth-century Saint Canice's Cathedral, where a one-hundred-foot intact Celtic round tower offers breathtaking views of the surrounding green countryside. Narrow covered alleyways known as 'slips' wind between historic stone taverns like Kyteler's Inn, while artisan workshops in the Kilkenny Design Centre celebrate Ireland's finest pottery, textiles, and silversmithing."
