      "title": "Dublin: The Desert Sanctuary",
      "summary": "Dublin: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 5",
      "content": "### Chapter 19: Dublin: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Dublin - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/dublin-character.jpg)\n\nStraddling the River Liffey as it flows into the Irish Sea, Dublin is a UNESCO City of Literature steeped in Viking origins and Georgian grandeur. The river is crossed by historic bridges, most famously the cast-iron Ha'penny Bridge, built in 1816, leading to the cobblestone quarter of Temple Bar and the medieval stone battlements of Dublin Castle.\n\n![Geographic location of Dublin in Ireland](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/dublin-map.png)\n\nSouth of the river, Dublin's grand Georgian squares—Merrion Square and Fitzwilliam Square—are lined with four-story red-brick townhouses famous for their ornate fanlight doorways painted in vibrant red, canary yellow, and emerald green. Inside Trinity College, the majestic barrel-vaulted Long Room of the Old Library holds two hundred thousand antique leather-bound volumes beneath the gaze of marble busts of world philosophers."
