      "summary": "Belfast: The Desert Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 5",
      "content": "### Chapter 20: Belfast: The Desert Sanctuary\n\n![Belfast - Iconic historic citadel view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/belfast-character.jpg)\n\nNestled at the mouth of the River Lagan where it opens into Belfast Lough, Belfast is a city of grand Edwardian architecture and proud shipbuilding heritage. In the heart of the city stands Belfast City Hall, a magnificent baroque revival palace of Portland stone crowned by a copper-green dome and surrounded by manicured public lawns.\n\n![Geographic location of Belfast in United Kingdom](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-05/images/belfast-map.png)\n\nAcross the river in the Titanic Quarter, the striking architectural icon of Titanic Belfast rises with jagged aluminum facades resembling ship's hulls, overlooking the historic slipways where the RMS Titanic was designed and launched. To the north, the basalt cliffs of Cavehill—often called Napoleon's Nose—offer sweeping vistas of the bustling lough, yellow shipyard gantry cranes, and rolling Antrim hills."
